{"tool_name":"export2graphlan","contents":["biocontainers","galaxy","bioschemas","biotools","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"export2graphlan","identifiers":[],"license":"MIT","summary":"Conversion software tool for annotating tree with graphlan","home_url":"https://github.com/segatalab/export2graphlan","keywords":[],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":1736},"biotools":{"id":"export2graphlan","home":"https://github.com/SegataLab/export2graphlan/","license":"MIT","summary":"export2graphlan is a conversion software tool for producing both annotation and tree file for GraPhlAn. In particular, the annotation file tries to highlight specific sub-trees deriving automatically from input file what nodes are important.","addition_date":"2021-05-26T19:54:25Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-06T14:08:22.989369Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Workflow"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:export2graphlan","credit":[{"email":"nicola.segata@unitn.it","name":"Segata Lab","note":"The computational metagenomics lab at the Dep. CIBIO, University of Trento","typeEntity":"Division","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://segatalab.cibio.unitn.it/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["API documentation"],"url":"https://github.com/SegataLab/export2graphlan/"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["clsiguret"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Conversion","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3434"}]}],"name":"export2graphlan","owner":"Kigaard","publication":[{"doi":"10.7717/peerj.1029","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2015 Asnicar et al.The increased availability of genomic and metagenomic data poses challenges at multiple analysis levels, including visualization of very large-scale microbial and microbial community data paired with rich metadata. We developed GraPhlAn (Graphical Phylogenetic Analysis), a computational tool that produces high-quality, compact visualizations of microbial genomes and metagenomes. This includes phylogenies spanning up to thousands of taxa, annotated with metadata ranging from microbial community abundances to microbial physiology or host and environmental phenotypes. GraPhlAn has been developed as an open-source command-driven tool in order to be easily integrated into complex, publicationquality bioinformatics pipelines. It can be executed either locally or through an online Galaxy web application. We present several examples including taxonomic and phylogenetic visualization of microbial communities, metabolic functions, and biomarker discovery that illustrate GraPhlAn's potential for modern microbial and community genomics.","authors":[{"name":"Asnicar F."},{"name":"Huttenhower C."},{"name":"Segata N."},{"name":"Tickle T.L."},{"name":"Weingart G."}],"citationCount":295,"date":"2015-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"PeerJ","title":"Compact graphical representation of phylogenetic data and metadata with GraPhlAn"},"pmcid":"PMC4476132","pmid":"26157614","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Biomarkers","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3360"},{"term":"Metabolomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3172"},{"term":"Taxonomy","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0637"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"export2graphlan","home":"https://bio.tools/export2graphlan","license":"MIT","summary":"export2graphlan is a conversion software tool for producing both annotation and tree file for GraPhlAn. In particular, the annotation file tries to highlight specific sub-trees deriving automatically from input file what nodes are important.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"galaxy":{"version":"@VERSION@+@GALAXY_VERSION@","first_commit":"2017-03-03","conda_name":"export2graphlan","conda_version":"0.22","summary":"export2graphlan is a conversion software tool for producing both annotation and tree file for GraPhlAn","edam_operations":["Conversion"],"edam_topics":["Taxonomy","Metabolomics","Biomarkers"],"toolshed_categories":["Metagenomics"],"toolshed_id":"export2graphlan","users_5_years":920,"users_all_time":1062,"usage_5_y